  "summary": "Denial of service on the CAN bus. During the 5.50s alert an injector flooded the bus with 0x000, the highest-arbitration-priority ID, which is absent from the baseline ID set: it sent 950 frames (172.73 msg/s, 28% of all alert traffic) with a constant all-zero payload, including back-to-back frames only ~0.44 ms apart. The effect is classic DoS starvation of legitimate traffic: all 26 countable baseline IDs ran below 70% of baseline rate, the ~100 Hz IDs (0x140, 0x350, 0x131, 0x370) dropped to roughly 0.22-0.24x baseline with mean gaps stretched from ~10 ms to ~43-45 ms, and 0x2B0 was silenced entirely (~550 expected frames never sent). Average bus load stayed below baseline (0.31x) because legitimate traffic collapsed, but the busiest 0.5s window reached 0.96x of baseline load, consistent with bursty high-priority injection that wins arbitration whenever it transmits. Spoofing/replay are ruled out because rate_inflation is 0.0 and no baseline ID exceeded baseline; fuzzing is ruled out because the only unknown ID carries a constant, not random, payload; and this is not the benign false-alarm pattern (timing/missing_ids/payload_entropy only), since unknown_ids is also elevated at 0.6 and the appearance of a non-baseline highest-priority ID coinciding with suppression of every other ID is not a normal vehicle state change.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The alert spans 28.75s to 34.25s (5.50s, 21 merged windows) and contains 3363 frames from 27 arbitration IDs, 1 of them absent from the baseline, with detector score 1.00.",
      "cites": ["E0"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The detector's elevated components are missing_ids 1.0, unknown_ids 0.6, timing 0.45 and payload_entropy 0.376, while rate_inflation and bus_load are both 0.0.",
      "cites": ["E0"]
    },
    {
      "text": "0x000 is not in the baseline ID set and sent 950 frames over the whole alert (172.73 msg/s) with payload entropy 0.000 bits, i.e. a constant payload.",
      "cites": ["E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sample frames show 0x000 carrying the all-zero payload 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00, with two 0x000 frames only about 0.44 ms apart, consistent with back-to-back burst injection.",
      "cites": ["E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Frames from IDs absent from the baseline (identified as 0x000) make up 950 of the 3363 frames in the alert (28%), and all 26 countable baseline IDs ran below 70% of their baseline rate.",
      "cites": ["E2", "E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ~100 Hz IDs 0x140, 0x350, 0x131 and 0x370 each ran at only 0.224x-0.236x of baseline over the alert, with mean inter-frame gaps stretched from ~10 ms to 42.6-44.9 ms (28.99-98.54 sigma), and each only momentarily reached its baseline rate (1.0x) in its peak window.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "0x5A2 ran at 0.18x of its baseline rate over the alert.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "0x2B0 sent nothing during the alert although the baseline expects about 550 frames in that time.",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Average bus load over the alert was 611 msg/s versus a 1953 msg/s baseline (0.31x), while its busiest 0.5s window reached 1868 msg/s (0.96x of baseline).",
      "cites": ["E1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No baseline ID ran above its baseline rate (rate_inflation 0.0 and all 26 baseline IDs below 70%), which rules out spoofing- or replay-style rate inflation.",
      "cites": ["E0", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The evidence does not identify the vehicle function of any affected ID; 0x140, 0x350, 0x131, 0x370, 0x5A2 and 0x2B0 are all listed with unknown function.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6", "E7", "E8", "E9"]
    }
  ],
  "recommended_action": "Treat as an active DoS injection. Identify and isolate the node or tool transmitting 0x000 (it is not part of the baseline ID set) and consider gateway/IDS allowlist filtering of 0x000. Verify whether the sender of 0x2B0 recovered after 34.25s and inspect the suppressed ECUs for dropped frames, queue overflows or error counters. Capture at finer time resolution to characterize the injection burst pattern and duty cycle, and preserve the trace for forensics."
}

